how young people can get respect  so i got a great question from one of my  newsletter readers trevor  love you guys who wrote in to say evan  in today's corporate world  if you're interested in advancement of  moving up it's not so much about how  good you are at your job or how hard you  work but how people see you  well it took me some time to come to  terms and realize this i must say it's a  constant battle  i graduated college in 2012 and  september took a job with the company  simply to make ends meet  i got an opportunity that gave me some  exposure and got promoted within three  months and then nine months later i got  promoted again  i love what i do my passion is to lead  people  and this allows me to do it however the  next step has much more to do with image  i'm 25  and i've met many people under me or  that are equal to me who are old enough  to be my parents  i tell you this simply because i was  wondering if you could do a video or  give  feedback on image in the corporate world  specifically around  how people above you below you and equal  do you see you  thanks to time my friend trevor trevor  this is a great question  and one that uh i struggled myself with  you know with all of my ventures  i was always the youngest person in the  room  and i was selling the people who were  way older than me  and at the beginning i had a really hard  time with it and so my three  bits of advice the first one for you is  have confidence  and this one was so hard for me at the  start i remember my first software  company i was 19 years old  and i was selling the people who were  three times my age and had phds and all  these  all this experience and i i was so  nervous and scared at the beginning like  well  like who am i compared to these guys  and then i realized that what i had  could help them  right i don't need to be the expert at  you know what they're an expert at but  my software my product  my service could help them do their job  better  and once i realized that and i had more  confidence going in  they could smell it right like they can  smell your confidence  and they're much more willing to listen  to you where if you come in and you're  afraid  and and you're not so sure they're gonna  think oh this young punk you know  wasting my time so one understand that  you are  talented you have skills you're gonna  help these people and it's not an ego  thing  it's not i'm the best you know i'm  amazing  screw you guys you know what you're  talking about i'm i'm the greatest thing  ever  that's not it it's just knowing deep  down inside  that you can help them you can help  these people do their jobs better  the second one is to remember that  respect is earned  right if you're managing somebody who is  old enough to be your parents  then they may start off with a little  bit of bias right like this young kid  is my boss tell me what to do but there  is a reason why you're there there's a  reason why you're their boss  and if you want to earn their respect  you want to talk about leading people  right leading  leadership is your passion leading  people is what you want to do  right respect is earned so  what can you do to earn people's respect  right  you got to show that you're working hard  right this this person is under you if  they're  having a hard time making a deadline  maybe you stayed late  and help them and you're working side by  side with them  right that's going to make them want to  work with you right that's going to make  them respect you  say wow this person is a good boss  so you got to earn their respect and  it's not by you sitting  on top of them and saying do this do  this do this  right i'm the greatest thing ever you  get down in the trenches  you work with them you show them why you  were hired  right you're leading from the front  you're going into battle with them so  quickly earn their respect  show them and then the third thing is  don't care so much  i know you think this is the end all  right like  it's all about it's not about how hard  you work and your skills is about how  people perceive you  i gotta tell you man stop caring as much  about what other people think about  yourself as long as you are playing  to other people's expectations of you  then you're never gonna realize your  full potential you're living somebody  else's dream  now here's a quick example okay when i  when i was super young  um somewhat i'm 30 well yeah i'm 34 now  so you know i'm still going into  meetings with people who are sometimes  twice my age  i'm not always english in the room but  often i'm still talking to people way  older than me  when i first started meeting people  clients  i used to always have a suit on i felt  like the suit made me more important  gave me more confidence it just gave me  a sense that you know i'm a little more  professional  and over the years i've dropped the suit  you know i went  down to business casual now almost  casual i'll go to meetings with the  belief shirt with my hoodie on  important meetings and they don't care  because i don't care right when you walk  in  and and you're so concerned about what  other people are thinking about you  it shows i promise you it shows they can  smell it  where if you walk in and again it's not  an ego thing it's not saying how great  you are  but you're not worried so much about  what other people are thinking  you're not worried about having a suit  on because  that makes you feel more important you  are important you feel important just  being you  and it doesn't matter what you're  wearing you got to get to that point  and i guarantee you when you get there  you'll have a lot more fun  you'll get promoted way faster  you will get way more results for your  company  so it's all internal and for young  people watching  because i had to battle this i had to  battle this in a really bad way when i  was first getting started  age is an issue but not nearly as big an  issue as you make it out to be  as long as you go in to any situation  feeling like you're being held back  because of your age  then that's going to be your reality  it's such a tiny  issue it's almost a non-issue  there are so many more important factors  so know that you're awesome feel it  be confident not from an ego point of  view again but just know  that you're really good at what you do  that you can really help and you don't  care so much  about how other people perceive you know  that  you're just as good as the people who  are two three times your  age if not better and if you go in with  that mindset and you actually feel it  it's not like  you got to sit in the washroom and tell  yourself before okay you know i'm really  good don't get nervous i'm really good  you're not you're not prepping yourself  out but you you you actually feel that  then they'll respect you and you'll get  faster promotions  and you get better results believe  those are watching if you have a story  to share about how you overcame  confidence issues or feeling like you're  too young  leave it in the comments below i want to  hear your story you guys like this video  thumbs up below  click on my face subscribe to the  channel thank you so much i'll see you  soon  you

